+    You can also filter groups based on their members using the
+    ``filter_groups`` parameter. This receives the complete member list
+    of each group once; retain that group only when its result is truthy.
+    ``None`` retains all groups.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        {# Only show cities with more than one person #}
+        <ul>{% for city, items in users|groupby("city", filter_groups=lambda x: len(x) > 1) %}
+          <li>{{ city }}: {{ items|length }} people</li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
     .. versionchanged:: 3.0
         Added the ``default`` parameter.
 
     .. versionchanged:: 2.6
         The attribute supports dot notation for nested access.
+
+    .. versionadded:: NEXTVERSION
+        Added the ``filter_groups`` parameter.
